[],0,82],[7147800,20404,2,0.13,0.082,[[8,39]],[],0,83],[7173603,20412,75,2.212,1.739,[[6,0.533,27,38],[11,0.402,4,34],[14,0.043,6,2],[9,0.022,9,1]],[["ea4ea741_c31851be",27,-1,1,"Should we start referencing this in `ProxyMain::IsRenderingPaused`? So that there is initial usage while you build the next steps above it?"],["a1baadb3_877485a0",28,0,0,"Does commenting out the name of the trace event break it?"]],0,84],[7187002,20416,121,2.212,1.739,[[8,0.976,40,119],[28,0.024,9,2]],[["39d176d3_3d9c1cfd",29,-3,1,"I would suggest defining the new macro in terms of `STATIC_HISTOGRAM_POINTER_GROUP` instead. This will remove the need to deal with do-while, atomics, etc. It would just be a thin layer that provides…"],["871a1a2a_d0858136",9,-3,1,"nit: \"to\""],["91135677_05f49608",29,-3,1,"I would suggest adding unit tests for the new macro. For example, it could test that, for each possible value from say -1 to 101, the histogram has the same behavior as…"],["d49b9ad0_a155d615",15,-3,1,"I think that the `Add(...)` could be pushed inside the macro as well, so that you just provide `percentage` here."],["e6856c26_6b191ca9",15,0,1,"This is also an old historgram we don't want to rebucket. Considering the analysis that we've done, we can remove this in a follow up actually"]],0,85],[7202423,20417,120,2.212,1.739,[[8,0.813,41,98],[3,0.187,7,22]],[["28d8200f_38514786",9,0,1,"Please fix this INFO reported by Metrics: The following histograms were removed without an obsoletion message: EventLatenc... The following histograms were removed without an obsoletion message:…"],["3576a04d_f2726980",15,0,1,"We can probably eliminate the enum and its usages as well"],["3632ac9e_3c3c3486",15,0,1,"Can we also remove the entries in `tools/metrics/histograms/metadata/event/histograms.xml` ?"],["fef27cf8_791dd88d",9,0,1,"Please fix this INFO reported by Metrics: The following histograms have been removed and obsoleted in this CL: EventLatenc... The following histograms have been removed and obsoleted in this CL:…"]],0,86],[7147802,20431,201,3.856,3.092,[[6,0.909,28,186],[17,0.053,8,9],[9,0.038,10,6]],[["2bc97bb3_a08a7dcf",28,-5,1,"Would we need a `BeginMainFrame` if we are paused? If so that is subtle and we should add a comment as to why"],["4f238514_b92fbd6d",28,-5,1,"The other aspect of this, is that when `new_state` is true, we want to recalculate these lambdas whenever their params change. As we would want to fire the idle signals then."],["7dada7e9_7a0da46a",28,-5,1,"Nit: use feature name"],["bcff8c3d_926dce69",28,-5,0,"Is this something we would want in `lambda_begin_frame_needed`?"],["2e820fe6_fd1ab8f6",28,0,0,"Mind filling a bug for follow up. I wonder if sending this when the `until` is really short is useful."],["a0729dae_707ecd91",28,0,1,"Nit: we shouldn't land commented out code. Having it tracked in the bugs SGTM"],["fbdefa57_51e4a04d",27,0,1,"These seem to be unused now?"]],0,87],[7242290,20432,13,0.394,0.273,[[6,29]],[],0,88],[7243392,20432,2,0.13,0.082,[[6,30]],[],0,89],[7248954,20433,11,0.406,0.291,[[8,42]],[],0,90],[7252610,20433,21,0.198,0.14,[[32,3]],[],0,91]]}